  "section_notes": "S1 requires 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents, which applies to both companies' unreported incidents. S2 keeps the 5% limit and customer access to per-model results but pauses new marketing on exceedance, with an open-ended regulator-authorised alternative; existing models are not expressly exempt, so the rating is weakened on the transition clause. S5 keeps the 8 per 100k mandatory recall trigger with no transition, which bears most heavily on Halcyon's Ember 8."
